  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Refugees in Kenya (2012-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide essential humanitarian assistance to save lives, relieve suffering, and maintain the dignity of Somali refugees in KenyaTo provide essential humanitarian assistance for up to 415,000 refugees in Kenya by ensuring improved access to clean water, sanitation, nutrition, health and protection services (e.g. police, secure accommodation for unaccompanied minors and victims of gender based violence). This will help save lives, relieve suffering, and maintain the dignity of refugees in Kenya.To provide essential humanitarian assistance for up to 535,000 refugees in Kenya by ensuring improved access to clean water, sanitation, nutrition, health and protection services (e.g. secure accommodation for unaccompanied minors and victims of gender based violence) and sustainable climate change interventions. This will help save lives, relieve suffering, and maintain the dignity of refugees in Kenya in a sustainable way.</narrative>
  </description>
